# Supabase project settings -> Database -> Connection string (URI, "Session pooler" tab).
# Use the POOLER host (aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com), not db.<ref>.supabase.co directly:
# the direct host is IPv6-only unless you've bought the IPv4 add-on, which fails DNS resolution
# on most home networks ("could not translate host name"). Pooler username is postgres.<project-ref>.
# Swap postgres:// for postgresql+psycopg2:// so SQLAlchemy picks the right driver.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://postgres.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[YOUR-REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# console.groq.com -> API Keys -> Create API Key. Used by agents/triage_agent.py (and
# every later specialist agent) via langchain-groq.
GROQ_API_KEY=[YOUR-GROQ-API-KEY]
# Optional: GROQ_API_KEY_2, _3, ... -- a separate Groq account's key, used as an automatic
# fallback once the active key hits its daily quota (see run_eval.py's _discover_api_keys).

# Signs/verifies this app's own JWTs (api/auth.py) -- not a Supabase key. Generate with:
# python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
JWT_SECRET=[GENERATE-YOUR-OWN-RANDOM-SECRET]